{
  "_provenance": [
    "KAN-501. One page of Jira comments as the Atlassian proxy receives it, inside",
    "the proxy envelope it is wrapped in.",
    "",
    "HOW IT WAS MADE, AND WHAT IS REAL IN IT. The envelope, the status and the `via`",
    "block are quoted verbatim from a live call made on 2026-08-18 against the fleet",
    "daemon at rung `confluence-write`:",
    "",
    "    atlassian_get_issue_comments({ issueKey: \"KAN-501\", maxResults: 1 })",
    "    -> completeness.unclippedChars 11626, body.chars 10682, body omitted for budget",
    "",
    "THE COMMENT BODY IS THE REAL TEXT of KAN-501 comment 12769, converted to ADF by",
    "this repository's own markdownToAdf. It is generated rather than captured FOR THE",
    "REASON THIS TICKET EXISTS: the proxy clips the body it is asked for, so the ADF it",
    "clips is the one payload no proxy call can hand back. The stand-in is CHECKED",
    "rather than assumed — section 0 of verify-clip-recipes-are-executable.mjs asserts",
    "that this object measures within 25% of the 10,682 characters the live call",
    "reported for the same comment, so a converter change that made the fixture",
    "unrepresentative goes red there rather than silently weakening every section",
    "below it. Measured when written: 9,198 against 10,682, or 86%. The shortfall is",
    "Jira's own ADF carrying marks and attrs this converter does not emit; it makes",
    "the fixture SMALLER than the real thing, which is the conservative direction —",
    "a defect that shows up on this fixture shows up on the real payload too.",
    "",
    "The author email is replaced with an invalid-domain placeholder. Nothing else is",
    "altered."
  ],
