          "content": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "attrs": {
                "level": 2
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Provenance, which sharpens this: the broken tool is the newest one, and it shipped with the brief change that tells agents to rely on it."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "task/KAN-420",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "code"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ", 2026-08-16."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "atlassian_get_issue_comments",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "code"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " was added by "
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "c9ce024",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "code"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " — \"KAN-471: the Jira comment read is a window, and its marker sits after the array that hides it (#207)\", 2026-08-15. Established by diffing the operation table: the proxy carried "
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "31",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "strong"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " operations before that commit and "
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "32",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "strong"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " after, and the one added is exactly this tool."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "That same commit is the last change to",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "strong"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " "
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "prompts/task.md",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "code"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ", which is what tells every agent:"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "blockquote",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Butchr's own proxy now carries "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "atlassian_get_issue_comments",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "code"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ", which pages the whole history by "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "startAt",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "code"
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "So the remedy and the instruction to use it shipped together, and neither was ever measured against a running daemon",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "strong"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " — because the proxy had never been switched on anywhere. KAN-420's ladder walk is the first time any of these 32 operations ran against the fleet's daemon, and this tool failed the first time it was asked."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Note the shape rather than blaming the commit.",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "strong"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " Nothing in KAN-471 is wrong in itself: the tool is correctly written, the pagination arguments are right, and against a raw Jira response it would do exactly what it says. The defect is the interaction with a response budget that lives in a different module and was not part of that change. "
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "It is the gap between two correct things, which is the failure mode this epic keeps re-finding",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "strong"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " — and it degraded toward looking finished, because the tool exists, is advertised, and returns "
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "success: true, status: 200",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "code"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Incidental correction for the record:",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "strong"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " KAN-420's own description states the surface as "
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "31 operations — 21 reads, 10 writes",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "em"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ". Measured off the running build it is "
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "32 — 22 reads, 10 writes",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "strong"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ". The count was correct when taken on 2026-08-14 and drifted by this one commit."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
